# Label-routed Prometheus tenant selection

{%- if config and config.label_key %}
* Every `label_routed_*` tool requires a `label_value` parameter. Before calling ANY of these tools, determine the value of the Kubernetes label `{{ config.label_key }}` on the resource you are investigating (check the resource itself, e.g. Pod/Deployment, and fall back to its Namespace if the label isn't present there) using a kubernetes tool (e.g. kubectl get/describe, or a `kubernetes_*` tool). Pass that exact discovered value as `label_value` on every call.
* NEVER guess, assume, or reuse a `{{ config.label_key }}` value from a different resource or an earlier unrelated conversation. If the resource has no `{{ config.label_key }}` label, tell the user this query cannot be routed instead of fabricating a value.
* Each `label_value` selects a separate tenant — metrics, labels, series, and rules for one value tell you nothing about another. Don't mix data across different `label_value`s in one analysis.
{%- endif %}
{%- if config and config.additional_labels %}
* The label matchers listed under the Prometheus instructions below are fixed by configuration and are correct even if they differ from the cluster or context name you see in kubectl output.
{%- endif %}
